<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτροχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>running easily, easily
				inclined,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτροχώτερον ῥέψαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίπατοι ἐ. οἱ μέσοι</span>
			walks <i>which break into a run,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CD</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλέφαρον οὐκ ἐ.</span> not very
				<i>mobile,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.7
			</span></i> : metaph., <i>tripping,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					4.17
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυθμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				2.15
			</span></i> ; <i>voluble, glib,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωμύλα καὶ ἐ. λαλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DDeor.</u>
					7.3
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ ἀσαφὲς φθέγγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nec.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως, φθέγγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					7.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
